        "original_id": "edef8124-28f8-5097-b84b-4d7e97f3db49",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Systems: Southern Railway, Semmering railway\n- Places: Austria, Vienna, Graz, Spielfeld, Slovenia, Semmering, Bruck an der Mur, Gloggnitz, Mürzzuschlag, Wien Liesing railway station\n\nFacts:\n- In 1841, Wien Liesing railway station opened together with the Southern Railway.\n- The Southern Railway in Austria runs from Vienna to Graz and to the Slovenia border at Spielfeld via Semmering and Bruck an der Mur.\n- The Semmering railway in Austria starts at Gloggnitz and leads over the Semmering to Mürzzuschlag.\n- The Semmering railway was the first mountain railway in Europe built with a standard-gauge track.",
